# VITE_API_BASE_URL: Base URL of the RiskSearcher backend API (FastAPI/persistent server).
# Set this in your local environment or deployment platform. Do not commit a
# production backend URL to source control.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=""

# Add any client-safe public keys here (e.g. WalletConnect Project ID, Circle publishable key).
# Never put server-side secrets (LLM API keys, Circle secret keys) in a VITE_-prefixed var —
# anything prefixed VITE_ is bundled into client-side JS and publicly readable.

# Circle Modular Wallets — passkey-backed ERC-4337 smart account (MSCA) on
# Arc Testnet. No OAuth app, no redirect URIs — just these two values.
# See services/passkeyWallet.ts.
# Client Key: Circle Developer Console > Keys > Create a key > Client Key
VITE_CIRCLE_CLIENT_KEY=""
# Fixed public endpoint — same for every app, no need to create anything.
VITE_CIRCLE_CLIENT_URL="https://modular-sdk.circle.com/v1/rpc/w3s/buidl"
# One more required one-time step (not an env var): Circle Developer
# Console > Wallets > Modular Wallets > Passkey — set the passkey domain
# to your deployed origin (e.g. risksearcher.vercel.app). Passkeys are
# domain-bound; this must be HTTPS (or localhost for local dev).
